{"insensitive_in_distributed_representations": "Insensitivity in distributed representations refers to the challenge that numerical values pose in natural language processing tasks, where they often lead to contradictions and are difficult to accurately represent and match across different data modalities like eligibility criteria and EHR."},
{"existing_patient_trial_matching_works": "Existing patient-trial matching works refer to the current methodologies and systems used to match patients with clinical trials based on eligibility criteria and patient electronic health records (EHR)."},
