{"machine_learning_and_rule_based_methods": "Machine learning and rule-based methods represent two different strategies for information extraction. Machine learning methods rely on algorithms that learn from data to make predictions or decisions, while rule-based methods use pre-defined rules and human annotations to extract information."},
{"criteria2query__forms__patient_criteria": "The predicate \"forms\" indicates that Criteria2Query is actively involved in structuring or organizing data into a specific format or criteria, in this case, patient criteria."},
{"patient_criteria": "Patient criteria refer to the specific conditions or parameters that define the eligibility of a patient for a clinical trial. These criteria are essential for matching patients to appropriate trials based on their medical profiles and the requirements of the trials."},
