{"bert__predicts__randomly_masked_words_in_a_sequence": "The action of predicting randomly masked words in a sequence is a key feature of BERT's training process. This technique, known as the Masked Language Model, involves randomly hiding some words in a sentence and then training the model to predict these hidden words based on the context provided by the surrounding words. This helps BERT to learn more robust and bidirectional representations of words."},
