{"clinical_trial_ec": "Clinical Trial EC refers to the process or dataset involving the extraction and analysis of eligibility criteria from clinical trials. It involves downloading XML files, selecting specific criteria, and extracting statements for further analysis."},
{"clinical_trial_ec__randomly_selected__794_clinical_trials": "The predicate \"randomly selected\" indicates that the clinical trials were chosen without any specific bias or preference, ensuring a diverse and representative sample for the study."},
{"794_clinical_trials": "The 794 clinical trials represent a subset of trials from ClinicalTrials.gov that were chosen for the study. These trials span various disease domains and were used to extract a total of 12,445 sentence-level eligibility criteria statements.|Here is another description: The 794 clinical trials represent a subset of trials chosen from ClinicalTrials.gov for analysis. These trials span various disease domains and are the source from which the XML files, containing the Inclusive and Exclusive Criteria, are downloaded and processed to extract the sentence-level EC statements."},
{"clinical_trials__have__varying_disease_domains": "The predicate \"have\" in this context indicates the possession or inclusion of a characteristic or feature within the clinical trials. It suggests that clinical trials encompass or are associated with a certain attribute."},
{"varying_disease_domains": "Varying disease domains refer to the different medical conditions or areas of health that clinical trials may focus on. These domains can include a wide range of diseases, such as cancer, cardiovascular diseases, neurological disorders, and more."},
{"clinical_trials__were_downloaded_from__clinicaltrials_gov": "The phrase \"were downloaded from\" indicates the action of obtaining or retrieving clinical trial data from a specific source. This action is crucial for researchers to access and analyze the data for further study."},
{"clinicaltrials_gov": "ClinicalTrials.gov is a registry and results database of privately and publicly funded clinical studies conducted around the world. It serves as a comprehensive resource for information on clinical trials, including their purpose, design, and outcomes."},
{"xml_files": "XML files in the context of clinical trials are digital documents that contain structured data about clinical trials. These files are essential for storing, sharing, and processing trial-related information in a standardized format.|Here is another description: XML files in this context are structured documents that store clinical trial descriptions. Each file adheres to a defined XML schema, organizing data into fields that can be systematically accessed and processed."},
{"xml_files__follow__a_fixed_structure_defined_by_the_clinical_trial_xml_schema": "The predicate \"follow\" indicates that the XML files adhere to or comply with a specific set of rules or guidelines. In this case, it means that the XML files are structured according to predefined standards."},
{"a_fixed_structure_defined_by_the_clinical_trial_xml_schema": "The fixed structure defined by the clinical trial XML schema is a standardized format that dictates how data within the XML files should be organized. This schema ensures consistency and interoperability of clinical trial data across different systems and platforms."},
{"we__select__inclusive_criteria_and_exclusive_criteria": "\"Select\" in this context means to choose or pick specific elements from a set of data. The researchers are choosing particular criteria from the clinical trial data to use in their study."},
{"inclusive_criteria_and_exclusive_criteria": "\"Inclusive Criteria and Exclusive Criteria\" are the specific sets of conditions or requirements that determine the eligibility of participants for a clinical trial. These criteria are selected by the researchers to form the raw data for their study on eligibility criteria (ECs)."},
{"raw_ecs": "Raw ECs refer to the initial, unprocessed data extracted from the Inclusive Criteria and Exclusive Criteria of clinical trials. These are the foundational elements from which more refined and structured information is derived."},
{"raw_ecs__form__from_inclusive_criteria_and_exclusive_criteria": "The predicate \"form\" in this context signifies the process of creating or generating raw ECs from the Inclusive Criteria and Exclusive Criteria. It indicates the transformation of structured criteria into raw, unstructured data."},
{"from_inclusive_criteria_and_exclusive_criteria": "Inclusive Criteria and Exclusive Criteria are predefined sets of conditions that determine the eligibility of participants for a clinical trial. These criteria are essential for ensuring that the trial is conducted with the appropriate subjects, thereby maintaining the validity and reliability of the trial results."},
{"ec_statements__extracted_through__patter_based_paragraph_segmentation_and_sentence_segmentation": "The predicate \"extracted through\" indicates the method or process used to obtain the EC statements. In this context, it refers to the specific techniques applied to derive these statements from the raw text data."},
{"patter_based_paragraph_segmentation_and_sentence_segmentation": "Pattern-based paragraph segmentation and sentence segmentation are techniques used to break down raw text into manageable segments. These methods involve identifying patterns within the text to separate it into paragraphs and then further into individual sentences, facilitating easier extraction and analysis of information."},
{"total_ec_statements_obtained": "The total number of EC (Eligibility Criteria) statements obtained refers to the cumulative count of sentence-level criteria extracted from the clinical trials' XML files. These statements are derived from the _Inclusive Criteria_ and _Exclusive Criteria_ sections of the trials."},
{"total_ec_statements_obtained__is__12_445": "The predicate \"is\" signifies the exact quantity or count of the EC statements that have been successfully extracted and compiled from the clinical trials' data."},
{"12_445": "The object \"12,445\" represents the total count of sentence-level EC statements that were extracted from the 794 selected clinical trials. This number is the result of processing the raw ECs through pattern-based segmentation techniques."},
{"sentence_level_ec_statements": "Sentence-level EC statements refer to the individual, discrete statements extracted from the eligibility criteria (EC) of clinical trials. These statements are derived from the raw ECs by segmenting paragraphs and sentences, providing a more granular view of the criteria."},
{"sentence_level_ec_statements__for__794_clinical_trials": "The predicate \"for\" in this context signifies the relationship between the sentence-level EC statements and the clinical trials they are associated with. It indicates that these statements are specifically generated or applicable to the selected clinical trials."},
{"large_scale_patient_trial_matching_data": "The Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data, also known as the IQVIA dataset, is a comprehensive dataset used for matching patients to clinical trials. It includes 561 registered clinical trials and 57,696 matched patients, with patient information encoded in longitudinal prescription and medical claims data.|Here is another description: The Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data is a comprehensive dataset used for training and validating models in the context of clinical trials. It includes 561 registered clinical trials and 57,696 matched patients, with patient information encoded in longitudinal prescription and medical claims data."},
{"large_scale_patient_trial_matching_data__is_used_for__model_training_and_validation": "The predicate \"is used for\" indicates the purpose or application of the Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data. In this context, it signifies that the dataset is utilized as a resource or tool for a specific function or process."},
{"model_training_and_validation": "Model training and validation refer to the processes of using data to train machine learning models and then assessing their performance to ensure they are accurate and reliable. In this context, the Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data is employed to train and validate models designed to match patients to clinical trials."},
{"large_scale_patient_trial_matching_data__is_also_known_as__iqvia_dataset": "The phrase \"is also known as\" indicates an alternative name or identifier for the subject. In this context, it signifies that the Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data has an alternative designation."},
{"iqvia_dataset": "The IQVIA dataset is an alternative name for the Large Scale Patient-Trial Matching Data. It is a dataset containing 561 registered clinical trials and 57,696 matched patients, utilized for model training and validation.|Here is another description: The IQVIA dataset is a large-scale trial-patient matched data used for model training and validation. It encompasses detailed patient information encoded in longitudinal prescription and medical claims data, alongside free-text eligibility criteria statements for each trial.|Here is another description: The IQVIA dataset is a large-scale dataset used for model training and validation in the context of clinical trial-patient matching. It encompasses a comprehensive collection of patient and trial data, including longitudinal prescription and medical claims data, as well as free-text eligibility criteria statements for each trial.|Here is another description: The IQVIA dataset is a comprehensive collection of medical and pharmaceutical data that includes a vast array of information on various health conditions, treatments, and patient data. It serves as a valuable resource for research and analysis in the healthcare industry, providing insights into patient outcomes, treatment efficacy, and market trends.|Here is another description: The IQVIA dataset is a collection of data used for evaluating the performance of algorithms like DeepEnroll. It serves as a standard benchmark in the context provided, allowing for a fair comparison of different systems based on their results on this dataset."},
{"iqvia_dataset__contains__561_registered_clinical_trials": "The predicate \"contains\" signifies that the IQVIA dataset includes or comprises a specific number of registered clinical trials within its framework, highlighting the dataset's scope and the breadth of clinical research it supports."},
{"561_registered_clinical_trials": "The 561 registered clinical trials represent a subset of the broader clinical research landscape encapsulated within the IQVIA dataset. These trials are accompanied by detailed eligibility criteria and matched patient data, providing a rich resource for analysis and model development."},
{"iqvia_dataset__contains__57_696_matched_patients": "The predicate \"contains\" in this context signifies that the IQVIA dataset includes or comprises a specific number of matched patients within its dataset. This indicates the dataset's scope and the volume of patient data it holds relevant to clinical trials."},
{"57_696_matched_patients": "The object \"57,696 matched patients\" refers to the total number of patients in the IQVIA dataset who have been successfully matched to clinical trials based on their electronic health records (EHR) and the trials' eligibility criteria. These matched patients represent a subset of the dataset that meets the specific requirements of the registered clinical trials."},
{"patient_information__is_encoded_in__large_scale_longitudinal_prescription_and_medical_claims_data": "The phrase \"is encoded in\" signifies that the patient information is systematically recorded and stored within a specific dataset or system. This encoding process involves converting the patient's health data into a structured format that can be analyzed and utilized for various purposes, such as research, treatment planning, or administrative functions."},
{"large_scale_longitudinal_prescription_and_medical_claims_data": "Large-scale longitudinal prescription and medical claims data represents a comprehensive dataset that tracks patients' medical prescriptions and claims over an extended period. This data includes detailed records of medications prescribed, medical procedures performed, and insurance claims submitted, providing a continuous and extensive view of patients' healthcare utilization and treatment history."},
{"each_trial": "Each trial refers to individual clinical trials within the IQVIA dataset, which is used for model training and validation. These trials are part of a larger collection of 561 registered clinical trials matched with 57,696 patients.|Here is another description: Each trial in this context refers to individual clinical studies designed to test the efficacy and safety of treatments for specific medical conditions, such as heart failure, Alzheimer\u2019s Disease, and idiopathic pulmonary fibrosis. These trials have specific eligibility criteria that patients must meet to participate.|Here is another description: Each trial refers to individual clinical trials that have been downloaded from a specific online database. These trials are part of a dataset used for data gathering and analysis."},
{"each_trial__has__a_number_of_free_text_ec_statements": "The predicate \"has\" indicates the relationship where each trial is associated with or includes a specific number of free-text EC (Eligibility Criteria) statements. These statements are essential for describing the requirements and conditions for patient participation in the trial."},
{"a_number_of_free_text_ec_statements": "A number of free-text EC statements are textual descriptions that outline the eligibility criteria for each clinical trial. These criteria cover various aspects of trial requirements and are crucial for determining whether a patient matches the trial's conditions."},
{"free_text_ec_statements": "Free-text EC statements are textual descriptions that provide detailed information about the eligibility criteria for clinical trials. They are part of the trial-patient matched data used for model training and validation."},
{"free_text_ec_statements__describe__trial_requirements_from_different_aspects": "The predicate \"describe\" indicates that the free-text EC statements provide a detailed account or explanation of the trial requirements. This relation highlights the role of these statements in conveying essential information about what is needed for patient participation in the trials."},
{"trial_requirements_from_different_aspects": "Trial requirements from different aspects refer to the various criteria and conditions that patients must meet to be eligible for a clinical trial. These requirements can include medical history, current health status, and other relevant factors that are outlined in the free-text EC statements."},
{"patients__are_profiled_as__a_set_of_ehr": "The profiling of patients as a set of EHR involves the systematic organization and representation of their medical history, diagnosis, and treatment records within an electronic health record system. This process allows for the assessment of patient eligibility for clinical trials based on their documented health data."},
{"a_set_of_ehr": "A set of EHR, in this context, refers to the comprehensive electronic health records of patients that include detailed records of their diagnoses and treatments. These records are crucial for evaluating patient suitability for clinical trials and for defining the entailment or contradiction of trial requirements."},
{"ehr__includes__records_of_diagnosis_and_treatments": "The term \"includes\" signifies that the subject, in this case, EHR, contains or encompasses certain elements. Here, it indicates that EHR comprises specific types of medical data."},
{"records_of_diagnosis_and_treatments": "Records of diagnosis and treatments are detailed documentations within EHR that outline the medical conditions diagnosed in patients and the treatments they have undergone or are currently receiving. These records are crucial for tracking patient health over time and for making informed medical decisions."},
{"inclusive_ec_and_exclusive_ec": "The inclusive EC and exclusive EC refer to the eligibility criteria used in clinical trials, which are described through free-text statements. These criteria are essential for determining patient eligibility based on their medical history and current health status."},
{"inclusive_ec_and_exclusive_ec__and_their_corresponding_matched_patients_ehr__are_defined_as_one_entailment_or_contradiction": "The relationship between the inclusive and exclusive EC and their corresponding matched patients\u2019 EHR involves evaluating how well the patient's electronic health records align with the trial's eligibility criteria. This alignment is crucial for determining whether a patient is a suitable match for a particular clinical trial."},
{"are_defined_as_one_entailment_or_contradiction": "The matched patients\u2019 EHR being defined as one 'Entailment' or 'Contradiction' signifies the outcome of the evaluation process. 'Entailment' indicates that the patient's EHR satisfies the trial's eligibility criteria, making them a suitable match. Conversely, 'Contradiction' means that the patient's EHR does not meet the criteria, disqualifying them from the trial."},
{"unmatched_ehr_and_ec_statements": "Unmatched EHR and EC statements refer to instances where electronic health record (EHR) data does not align with electronic consent (EC) data. These discrepancies are identified and categorized separately."},
{"unmatched_ehr_and_ec_statements__were_labelled_as__neutral": "The predicate \"were labelled as\" indicates the process of categorizing or tagging the unmatched EHR and EC statements with a specific label to facilitate further analysis or processing."},
{"total_labelled_examples": "The total labelled examples refer to the comprehensive count of instances that have been categorized or marked with specific labels in a dataset. This includes examples that have been reviewed and assigned a label based on certain criteria or attributes."},
{"total_labelled_examples__is__852_1031": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the state of being or the total count of the subject. It indicates that the number following it represents the complete quantity of the labelled examples."},
{"852_1031": "The number 852,1031 represents the total count of labelled examples in the dataset. This figure is the sum total of all instances that have been processed and assigned a label, reflecting the extent of the dataset's coverage in terms of labelled data."},
{"rare_disease_data": "The rare disease data refers to a specific collection of information within the broader IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed as rare diseases by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). This data subset includes details from 77 trials and information on 562 patients who match the criteria for these rare conditions.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset derived from the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions that are classified as rare. It is utilized for research and analysis of rare medical conditions.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset of the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). It serves as a critical resource for research and analysis specific to rare diseases.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset of the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). It is utilized for research and analysis specific to rare diseases.|Here is another description: Rare disease data refers to a dataset that contains information about diseases that affect a small percentage of the population. Evaluating DeepEnroll on this type of data is important to assess its capability in managing and providing insights from less common and more complex medical conditions."},
{"rare_disease_data__is_a_subset_of__iqvia_dataset": "\"Is a subset of\" indicates that the rare disease data is a smaller, specific part of a larger collection. In this context, it means that the rare disease data is contained within and is a part of the larger IQVIA dataset, which includes a wide range of medical and pharmaceutical data."},
{"rare_disease_data__contains_conditions_from__rare_diseases_list": "The phrase \"contains conditions from\" indicates that the rare disease data includes specific medical conditions that are listed in a designated source, in this case, the rare diseases list provided by NORD."},
{"rare_diseases_list": "The rare diseases list is a comprehensive compilation maintained by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). It serves as a reference for identifying and categorizing diseases that affect a small percentage of the population, thus qualifying them as rare.|Here is another description: The rare diseases list is a compilation of medical conditions that are considered rare, meaning they affect a small percentage of the population. This list is crucial for identifying and categorizing conditions that require specialized attention and research."},
{"rare_diseases_list__provided_by__national_organization_for_rare_disorders_nord": "The phrase \"provided by\" indicates the source or authority that has compiled, maintained, or officially recognized the rare diseases list. It signifies the entity responsible for the accuracy and credibility of the information contained within the list."},
{"national_organization_for_rare_disorders_nord": "The National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD) is a patient advocacy organization dedicated to individuals with rare diseases and the organizations that serve them. NORD is committed to the identification, treatment, and cure of rare disorders through programs of education, advocacy, research, and patient services."},
{"rare_disease_data__results_in__77_trials": "The phrase \"results in\" indicates the outcome or consequence derived from utilizing the rare disease data. In this context, it signifies the number of trials that were conducted or identified using this specific dataset."},
{"77_trials": "The 77 trials represent the total number of clinical trials that were either conducted or identified through the analysis of the rare disease data subset from the IQVIA dataset. These trials are crucial for advancing research and treatment options for rare diseases."},
{"rare_disease_data__results_in__562_matched_patients_from_iqvia_dataset": "The phrase \"results in\" indicates the outcome or the number of matches derived from applying the rare disease data subset to the broader IQVIA dataset. It signifies the effectiveness or yield of using this specific data subset in identifying relevant cases."},
{"562_matched_patients_from_iqvia_dataset": "The 562 matched patients from the IQVIA dataset represent the specific individuals whose data aligns with the criteria set by the rare disease data subset. These matches are crucial for further research, clinical trials, and understanding the prevalence and characteristics of rare diseases within the dataset."},
{"synthetic_data__developed_for__reproducibility": "The predicate \"developed for\" indicates the purpose or goal for which the synthetic data was created. It highlights the intention behind the generation of synthetic data, which in this case is to achieve reproducibility in studies and analyses."},
{"reproducibility": "Reproducibility in this context refers to the ability to replicate research findings or results consistently across different studies or analyses. It is a critical aspect of scientific research, ensuring that results are reliable and can be verified by others."},
{"synthetic_data__based_on__36": "The phrase \"based on\" indicates that the Synthetic Data is derived or modeled according to the principles, methods, or frameworks described in reference [36]. This suggests that the creation of the synthetic data follows a specific protocol or guideline outlined in the cited source."},
