{"synthea_3": "Synthea [3] is a synthetic patient population simulator that is used to automatically generate electronic health records (EHR). It is employed in this context to create a large dataset of simulation EHRs for research purposes."},
{"synthea": "Synthea is a tool used for generating synthetic data, specifically designed to create realistic patient Electronic Health Records (EHRs) for research and testing purposes."},
