{"a_synthetic_patient_population_simulator": "A synthetic patient population simulator is a type of software designed to generate artificial but realistic patient data. This data can be used for various purposes such as testing healthcare systems, training medical professionals, or conducting research without using real patient information."},
{"synthetic_data__used_to_generate__patient_ehr": "The predicate \"used to generate\" indicates the process by which Synthetic Data is employed to create or produce something. Here, it specifically refers to the utilization of synthetic data to automatically generate patient Electronic Health Records (EHR)."},
{"patient_ehr": "Patient EHR, or Electronic Health Records, are digital versions of patients' paper charts. They contain comprehensive medical and treatment histories of patients, including demographics, progress notes, problems, medications, vital signs, past medical history, immunizations, laboratory data, and radiology reports. In this context, patient EHRs are generated using synthetic data to simulate real patient records for analysis and testing purposes."},
{"we__select__243_registered_trials": "The predicate \"select\" indicates the action taken by the subject to choose or pick out a specific number of registered trials from a larger set for the purpose of the study."},
{"243_registered_trials": "The object \"243 registered trials\" represents the specific number of clinical trials that were chosen by the researchers from a wide range of disease domains to be included in the study for generating cohort definitions and filtering matched patient EHRs.|Here is another description: The subject refers to a collection of 243 registered trials, which are part of a study or research effort. These trials are significant as they represent a substantial dataset used for further analysis or simulation."},
