{"a_wide_range_of_disease_domains": "The object \"a wide range of disease domains\" describes the diverse medical fields or conditions that the 243 registered trials cover. This range implies that the trials are not limited to a single disease or medical area but span multiple domains, enhancing the comprehensiveness of the research or simulation."},
{"we__leverage__criteria2query": "\"Leverage\" in this context means to utilize or make use of a specific tool or resource to achieve a particular goal or enhance the research process."},
{"criteria2query__to_generate__cohort_definitions": "The predicate \"to generate\" in this context refers to the action performed by Criteria2Query, which involves creating or producing something. Specifically, it denotes the process by which Criteria2Query transforms input criteria into actionable queries that can be used to filter and select relevant data from a larger set of electronic health records."},
{"cohort_definitions": "Cohort definitions in this context refer to the specific sets of criteria or parameters used to identify and select a group of patients from electronic health records. These definitions are crucial for research studies or clinical trials, as they help in ensuring that the selected patient data is relevant and meets the necessary conditions for the study.|Here is another description: Cohort definitions refer to the specific criteria or parameters used to identify and select a group of patients from electronic health records (EHRs) for a particular study or analysis. These definitions are crucial for ensuring that the selected patient population is relevant and appropriate for the research question at hand."},
{"cohort_definitions__for__filtering_matched_patient_ehrs": "The predicate \"for\" in this context indicates the purpose or intended use of the cohort definitions. It signifies that the cohort definitions are specifically designed and applied to serve a particular function, which in this case is the filtering of matched patient EHRs."},
{"filtering_matched_patient_ehrs": "Filtering matched patient EHRs involves the process of selecting and isolating electronic health records that meet certain predefined criteria or match specific characteristics. This process is essential for creating a targeted dataset that is relevant to the research or analysis being conducted, ensuring that the data used is both accurate and pertinent to the study's objectives."},
{"we__have__68_845_simulation_ehrs": "The predicate \"have\" indicates possession or the result of an action performed by the subject, in this case, the creation and accumulation of a specific number of simulation EHRs."},
{"68_845_simulation_ehrs": "The object \"68,845 simulation EHRs\" represents the total number of electronic health records that were synthetically generated for the study, using a simulator to mimic real patient data across various disease domains.|Here is another description: The subject refers to a dataset comprising 68,845 simulation Electronic Health Records (EHRs) generated using Synthea, a synthetic patient population simulator. These records were created based on 243 registered trials across various disease domains."},
{"68_845_simulation_ehrs__labelled_in__similar_way_as_iqvia_dataset": "The predicate indicates that the 68,845 simulation EHRs have been labelled in a manner consistent with another dataset, specifically the IQVIA dataset. This suggests a methodological alignment in data labelling practices."},
