{"a_softmax_classifier": "The softmax classifier is a type of classifier that takes the output from the top layer of the MLP and converts it into a probability distribution over possible classes. It is used to make the final prediction in the model by determining the most likely class for the given input."},
{"long_short_term_memory_lstm": "Long Short Term Memory (LSTM) is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) designed to learn long-term dependencies. It is particularly effective in handling sequence prediction problems where the context or information from previous steps is crucial."},
