{"to_model_both_premise_sequence_and_hypothesis_sequence": "Modeling both premise sequence and hypothesis sequence involves using LSTM to understand and represent the input data in a structured form. This allows the model to capture the relationships and dependencies within the sequences, which is essential for tasks like natural language inference."},
{"lstm": "LSTM, or Long Short-Term Memory, is a type of recurrent neural network (RNN) architecture designed to better capture long-term dependencies in sequential data, commonly used in natural language processing tasks to maintain context over long sequences and mitigate issues like vanishing gradients."},
{"lstm__is_used_for__entailment_prediction": "The phrase \"is used for\" indicates the purpose or application of the subject. In this context, it specifies that LSTM is employed as a tool or method to achieve a particular task."},
{"entailment_prediction": "Entailment prediction refers to the task of determining whether a given hypothesis can be logically inferred from a premise. This is a common challenge in natural language processing, often addressed using machine learning techniques like LSTMs."},
{"match_lstm_mlstm": "Match-LSTM (mLSTM) is a specific type of Long Short-Term Memory network designed to handle natural language processing tasks. It is tailored to compare and analyze text data by focusing on the sequential nature of words."},
{"match_lstm_mlstm__perform__word_by_word_matching_of_the_hypothesis_with_the_premise": "The term \"perform\" in this context refers to the action or function that the match-LSTM (mLSTM) executes. It indicates that the mLSTM is actively engaged in carrying out a specific task related to text analysis."},
