{"free_text_eligibility_criteria": "The free-text eligibility criteria are the unstructured textual descriptions that outline the requirements or conditions for patient participation in clinical trials. These criteria are initially in a raw, unformatted state before being processed by the pipeline.|Here is another description: Free-text eligibility criteria refer to the textual descriptions of the conditions and requirements that participants must meet to be eligible for a clinical trial. These criteria are often written in natural language and can vary widely in format and detail."},
