{"multi_label_classification_task": "A multi-label classification task is a type of machine learning problem where each instance can be associated with multiple labels or categories. Unlike single-label classification, where each instance is assigned to one and only one class, multi-label classification allows for the possibility of an instance belonging to several classes simultaneously."},
{"micro_f1": "Micro-F1 is a specific type of F1 score used in multi-label classification tasks. It calculates the F1 score by considering the total true positives, false positives, and false negatives across all labels.|Here is another description: Micro-F1 is a specific method of calculating the F1 score in multi-label classification tasks. It considers the total true positives, false positives, and false negatives across all classes to provide a global view of performance, rather than treating each label independently."},
