{"soft_alignment_attention_weights": "Soft-alignment attention weights are numerical values that indicate the degree of relevance or importance assigned to different elements in a comparison or matching process. In the context of clinical trials, these weights help in understanding how well patient characteristics align with the eligibility criteria of a trial.|Here is another description: Soft-alignment attention weights are numerical values that indicate the degree of relevance or importance between different elements in a dataset. In the context of matching patients to clinical trials, these weights help determine how well a patient's characteristics align with the eligibility criteria of a trial."},
