{"weighted_average_of_attention_weights": "The weighted average of attention weights refers to the calculated mean of the soft-alignment attention weights collected for each trial. These weights signify the relevance or importance of various electronic health record (EHR) elements in relation to eligibility criteria (EC) statements for clinical trials."},
{"weighted_average_of_attention_weights__leveraged_into__patient_level_\u03b2": "The phrase \"leveraged into\" describes the process of utilizing or applying the weighted average of attention weights to derive meaningful insights or outcomes. In this context, it involves using the calculated average to understand the impact of EC statements on patient enrollment in clinical trials."},
