{"dark_color": "Dark color in the context refers to the visual representation used in heatmaps to indicate certain levels of data. Specifically, it is used to show the soft-alignment attention weights between electronic health records (EHR) and eligibility criteria (EC) in clinical trials.|Here is another description: Dark color in the heatmap represents areas where the attention weights are higher, suggesting a greater focus or significance in the context of EC statements and patient pairs."},
