{"heatmap__represents__attention_weights_for_ec_statements_and_patient_pairs": "The predicate \"represents\" indicates that the heatmap serves as a graphical depiction of the attention weights. It conveys how these weights are distributed across EC statements and patient pairs, providing a clear and intuitive understanding of the data."},
{"attention_weights_for_ec_statements_and_patient_pairs": "The attention weights for EC statements and patient pairs are values that indicate the level of relevance or importance assigned to each EC statement for a given patient. These weights are crucial for understanding how well a patient matches the criteria of a trial, as indicated by the EC statements."},
