{"trial__named__blitz_heart_failure_nct03661060": "The predicate \"named\" indicates that the trial has been given a specific designation or title. This naming is crucial for identifying and referencing the trial in discussions, databases, and research contexts."},
{"blitz_heart_failure_nct03661060": "BLITZ Heart Failure (NCT03661060) is the specific name and identifier given to the trial. This name and identifier are used to uniquely identify the trial in clinical databases and research literature, allowing for clear communication and reference among researchers and medical professionals.|Here is another description: BLITZ Heart Failure (NCT03661060) is a clinical trial focused on heart failure patients. It is specifically chosen for analysis due to its lower than 30% correct patient-trial matching using machine learning models."},
{"blitz_heart_failure_nct03661060__is__an_observational_study": "The predicate \"is\" in this context signifies the nature or type of the BLITZ Heart Failure trial, categorizing it within a specific research methodology."},
{"an_observational_study": "An observational study is a type of research where investigators assess health outcomes in groups of individuals without altering who receives the experimental treatment. In the case of BLITZ Heart Failure, it involves evaluating a structured approach to patient care."},
{"observational_study": "The observational study in question is the BLITZ Heart Failure trial (NCT03661060), which is a clinical trial aimed at analyzing patient data without intervention."},
{"observational_study__designed_to__evaluate_whether_a_structured": "The phrase \"designed to\" indicates the purpose or goal of the observational study, specifically what it aims to assess or investigate."},
{"evaluate_whether_a_structured": "The structured evaluation in the context of the BLITZ Heart Failure trial refers to a systematic approach or framework intended to assess a specific hypothesis or research question within the study."},
{"deepenroll__encodes__enrollment_criteria_and_patients_records_into_a_shared_latent_space": "The term \"encodes\" in this context refers to the process by which DeepEnroll transforms and represents enrollment criteria and patient records in a unified, abstract form that can be efficiently used for matching purposes."},
{"enrollment_criteria_and_patients_records_into_a_shared_latent_space": "Enrollment criteria and patients records into a shared latent space represent the diverse data inputs that DeepEnroll processes. These include textual descriptions of clinical trials and sequential data from patient electronic health records, which are crucial for accurate patient-trial matching."},
{"deepenroll__applies__a_pre_trained_bert_model_to_encode_clinical_trial_information": "The predicate \"applies\" in this context signifies the utilization or implementation of a specific method or model by DeepEnroll to process and encode information relevant to clinical trials and patient records."},
{"a_pre_trained_bert_model_to_encode_clinical_trial_information": "A pre-trained BERT model is a sophisticated natural language processing tool that has been trained on a large corpus of text data. In the context of DeepEnroll, it is used to encode clinical trial information, transforming textual data into a format that can be effectively analyzed and matched with patient records."},
{"deepenroll__uses__a_hierarchical_model_to_embed_patient_ehr": "The term \"uses\" in this context signifies the application or employment of a specific method or model by DeepEnroll to achieve its objective of encoding and matching patient records with clinical trial data."},
{"a_hierarchical_model_to_embed_patient_ehr": "A hierarchical model to embed patient EHR refers to a structured approach used by DeepEnroll to represent patient electronic health records (EHR) in a way that captures the complexity and relationships within the data, enabling effective matching with clinical trial information."},
{"deepenroll__is_augmented_by__a_numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module": "The phrase \"is augmented by\" indicates that DeepEnroll incorporates additional components or modules to enhance its functionality. In this context, it signifies that DeepEnroll has been improved or extended with extra features to better perform its intended task."},
{"a_numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module": "A numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component added to DeepEnroll to specifically handle and match numerical data within enrollment criteria (EC) and electronic health records (EHR). This module is designed to explicitly process and align numerical information, which is critical for accurate patient-trial matching."},
{"numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module__matches__numerical_information_in_ec_and_ehr": "The predicate \"matches\" indicates a process where the numerical information embedding and entailment module aligns and compares numerical data. This comparison is crucial for ensuring that the numerical values from different datasets are consistent and can be used effectively for patient-trial matching."},
{"deepenroll__was_evaluated_on__both_real_world_clinical_trial_dataset_and_a_synthetic_data": "The predicate \"was evaluated on\" indicates that DeepEnroll underwent testing and assessment to determine its effectiveness and performance. This evaluation process is crucial to validate the model's capabilities and ensure its reliability in practical applications."},
{"both_real_world_clinical_trial_dataset_and_a_synthetic_data": "The objects of evaluation for DeepEnroll include both a real-world clinical trial dataset and a synthetic data set. The real-world dataset consists of actual clinical trial data, providing a realistic testing environment. The synthetic data set, on the other hand, is artificially generated to simulate clinical trial scenarios, offering an additional layer of evaluation for the model."},
{"experiments_on_real_world_datasets": "Experiments on real-world datasets refer to the practical evaluations conducted using actual clinical trial data and patient records to test the effectiveness of the proposed model."},
{"experiments_on_real_world_datasets__demonstrated__the_strong_performance_of_deepenroll": "The term 'demonstrated' indicates that the experiments provided clear evidence or proof of a certain capability or performance."},
{"the_strong_performance_of_deepenroll": "The strong performance of DeepEnroll refers to the effectiveness and efficiency of the DeepEnroll model in accurately matching patients with clinical trials based on the encoded information from both enrollment criteria and patient records."},
{"deepenroll_method": "DeepEnroll is a cross-modal inference learning model designed to encode enrollment criteria and patient records into a shared latent space, facilitating patient-trial matching. It utilizes a pre-trained BERT model for clinical trial information and a hierarchical model for embedding patient EHR, augmented by a numerical information embedding and entailment module."},
{"deepenroll_method__can_be_extended_to__other_application_domains_for_matching_problems_based_on_heterogeneous_data": "The phrase \"can be extended to\" indicates the potential adaptability and versatility of the DeepEnroll method. It suggests that the method is not limited to its primary application in patient-trial matching but can be modified and applied to other areas that involve matching problems."},
{"other_application_domains_for_matching_problems_based_on_heterogeneous_data": "Other application domains for matching problems based on heterogeneous data refer to various fields where data of different types and sources need to be matched. Examples include personalized targeted advertising, where text-based ad descriptions are matched with sequential customer browsing history, demonstrating the method's broad applicability beyond healthcare."},
{"other_application_domains": "Other application domains refer to various fields or areas where a particular technology, method, or system can be applied beyond its primary use case. In the context of the paper, these domains are areas where the DeepEnroll method can be utilized for matching problems involving heterogeneous data."},
{"other_application_domains__include__personalized_targeted_advertising_based_on_matching_ads_description_and_customers_browsing_history": "The predicate \"include\" signifies that the subject encompasses or contains the object as a part of its broader applications or use cases. It indicates that the object is one of the specific instances or examples where the subject can be effectively applied."},
{"personalized_targeted_advertising_based_on_matching_ads_description_and_customers_browsing_history": "Personalized targeted advertising based on matching Ads description and customers\u2019 browsing history is a specific application where ads are tailored to individual users by analyzing the text descriptions of ads and the sequential data of users' browsing activities. This approach aims to deliver more relevant ads to users by understanding their interests and behaviors through their browsing history."},
{"this_work": "This work refers to a specific research project or academic endeavor that has received financial backing to support its activities and objectives.|Here is another description: This work refers to a research project or study that has received financial support from various funding bodies."},
