{"deepenroll__is_augmented_by__a_numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module": "The phrase \"is augmented by\" indicates that DeepEnroll's capabilities or functionalities are enhanced or extended through the integration of an additional component. In this case, the augmentation involves the incorporation of a specific module designed to handle numerical information.|Here is another description: The phrase \"is augmented by\" indicates that DeepEnroll incorporates additional components or modules to enhance its functionality. In this context, it signifies that DeepEnroll has been improved or extended with extra features to better perform its intended task."},
{"a_numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module": "A numerical information embedding and entailment module is a specialized component within DeepEnroll that is responsible for encoding and reasoning over numerical data extracted from textual inputs. This module facilitates the explicit matching of numerical information between textual data and EHR, enhancing the system's overall performance in data processing and analysis.|Here is another description: A numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component added to DeepEnroll to specifically handle and match numerical data within enrollment criteria (EC) and electronic health records (EHR). This module aims to improve the accuracy of matching by explicitly considering numerical values, which are critical in clinical contexts."},
{"numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module": "The numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component of DeepEnroll designed to handle numerical data within textual inputs. It creates a specialized numerical representation for encoding numbers found in text.|Here is another description: The numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component added to DeepEnroll to explicitly match numerical information representations and reason over numerical data in electronic health records and clinical trials. This module helps in enhancing the accuracy and effectiveness of the matching process by specifically addressing numerical data.|Here is another description: The numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component of the DeepEnroll framework designed to handle numerical data within clinical trial information and patient health records. It works alongside other modules to improve the accuracy of matching and reasoning processes.|Here is another description: The numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component within the DeepEnroll framework designed to handle and process numerical data. Its role is to match numerical information representations and integrate them into the overall framework.|Here is another description: The numerical information embedding and entailment module is a component of the DeepEnroll model designed to handle numerical data within clinical trial enrollment criteria and electronic health records."},
{"numerical_information_embedding_and_entailment_module__is_used_for__explicitly_reason_over_numbers": "The phrase \"is used for\" indicates the purpose or function of the numerical information embedding and entailment module within the system. It specifies the module's role in processing numerical information."},
{"explicitly_reason_over_numbers": "Explicitly reasoning over numbers involves the detailed and clear interpretation and comparison of numerical data extracted from text. This process allows for more accurate inferences and matching results between textual numerical information and electronic health records."},
{"deepenroll__proposes__a_numerical_representation_to_specifically_encode_numbers_in_textual_input_ec": "The action 'proposes' indicates that DeepEnroll suggests or puts forward a specific method or representation. In this context, it is suggesting a new way to handle numerical data within textual inputs."},
{"a_numerical_representation_to_specifically_encode_numbers_in_textual_input_ec": "The numerical representation proposed by DeepEnroll is designed to specifically encode numbers within textual input. This encoding is referred to as EC (Enrollment Code) and is intended to facilitate the extraction and comparison of numerical information from free-text inputs and electronic health records (EHR)."},
{"pattern_based_comparison_algorithm": "The pattern-based comparison algorithm is a method designed to process and analyze textual data, specifically focusing on numerical information within the text.|Here is another description: The pattern-based comparison algorithm is a method designed to handle and analyze numerical data within textual inputs, specifically in the context of electronic communications (EC) and electronic health records (EHR)."},
{"pattern_based_comparison_algorithm__is_developed_for__extracting_numbers_from_free_text_ecs": "The phrase \"is developed for\" indicates the purpose or application for which the pattern-based comparison algorithm was created. It suggests that the algorithm was specifically engineered to address a particular need or problem, in this case, related to extracting and comparing numerical data from text."},
{"extracting_numbers_from_free_text_ecs": "Extracting numbers from free-text ECs refers to the process of identifying and isolating numerical values within unstructured text, such as electronic communications (ECs), which may contain a mix of text and numbers without a predefined format."},
{"pattern_based_comparison_algorithm__is_developed_for__inference_between_extracted_numerical_information_in_ec_and_ehr": "The phrase \"is developed for\" indicates the purpose or application for which the pattern-based comparison algorithm was created. In this context, it signifies that the algorithm was specifically engineered to address the task of extracting and comparing numerical information between EC and EHR systems."},
{"inference_between_extracted_numerical_information_in_ec_and_ehr": "Inference between extracted numerical information in EC and EHR refers to the process of drawing conclusions or making deductions based on the numerical data that has been extracted from electronic communications and electronic health records. This involves analyzing the numbers to understand relationships, patterns, or discrepancies between the two data sources."},
{"comparison_results": "The comparison results refer to the outcomes generated by the pattern-based comparison algorithm, which involves extracting and inferring numerical information from textual input and electronic health records."},
