{"an_end_to_end_deep_learning_model": "An end-to-end deep learning model refers to a type of machine learning architecture that processes raw data through multiple layers of abstraction to produce a final output, without the need for manual feature engineering. DeepEnroll utilizes this approach to enhance patient-trial matching efficiency and accuracy."},
{"deepenroll__achieves__significantly_better_performance": "The predicate \"achieves\" in this context signifies that DeepEnroll has been evaluated and found to perform exceptionally well in its designated task. This performance metric is crucial as it demonstrates the model's effectiveness compared to other existing methods."},
{"significantly_better_performance": "\"Significantly better performance\" refers to the superior results obtained by DeepEnroll when compared to other patient-trial matching models. This improvement is evidenced through experimental evaluations, showcasing its enhanced capability in accurately and efficiently matching patients to clinical trials."},
