{"a_sequence_of_hospital_visits": "A sequence of hospital visits represents an ordered list of a patient's encounters with healthcare facilities, each visit containing specific diagnosis codes and associated treatments."},
{"each_hospital_visit": "Each hospital visit refers to a single instance of a patient being admitted to a hospital for medical care. This visit is part of a sequence that constitutes the patient's electronic health record (EHR) data."},
{"each_hospital_visit__consists_of__a_major_diagnosis_code_and_a_set_of_associated_treatments": "The phrase \"consists of\" indicates that each hospital visit is made up of or includes specific components. In this context, it means that a hospital visit is not a singular event but a composite of various medical assessments and interventions."},
{"a_major_diagnosis_code_and_a_set_of_associated_treatments": "A major diagnosis code is a standardized code used to classify the primary medical condition a patient is being treated for during a hospital visit. The set of associated treatments includes all the medications and procedures administered to the patient as part of their care for that visit."},
