{"set_of_ehr": "A set of EHR (Electronic Health Records) includes comprehensive records of a patient's diagnosis and treatments, which are used to profile patients for clinical trial matching. This structured data allows for the assessment of whether a patient meets the inclusion or exclusion criteria of a trial."},
{"ehr__includes__records_of_diagnosis_and_treatments": "The term 'includes' in this context signifies that EHR contains or encompasses specific types of medical data. It indicates that the EHR system is designed to store and manage various categories of patient information."},
{"records_of_diagnosis_and_treatments": "Records of diagnosis and treatments refer to the documented medical assessments and the therapeutic interventions provided to patients. These records are crucial for tracking patient health status, treatment efficacy, and for making informed clinical decisions."},
{"inclusive_ec_and_exclusive_ec": "The inclusive EC and exclusive EC refer to the criteria used in clinical trials to determine patient eligibility. These criteria are described in free-text statements that outline the requirements for participation in a trial.|Here is another description: Inclusive EC and exclusive EC refer to the criteria used in clinical trials to determine patient eligibility based on their electronic health records (EHR). These criteria are essential for matching patients to appropriate trials."},
{"inclusive_ec_and_exclusive_ec__matched_with__patients_ehr": "The relation \"matched with\" indicates the process of aligning or correlating the eligibility criteria (both inclusive and exclusive) of clinical trials with the electronic health records (EHR) of patients. This matching is essential for determining whether a patient meets the criteria to participate in a specific trial."},
