{"rare_disease_data": "The rare disease data refers to a specific collection of information within the broader IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed as rare diseases by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). This data subset includes details from 77 clinical trials and information on 562 patients who match the criteria for these rare conditions.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset derived from the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions that are classified as rare. It is utilized for research and analysis of rare medical conditions.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset of the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). It serves as a valuable resource for researchers and clinicians studying uncommon medical conditions.|Here is another description: The rare disease data is a specialized subset of the IQVIA dataset, focusing on conditions listed by the National Organization for Rare Disorders (NORD). It is used for research and analysis specific to rare diseases.|Here is another description: Rare disease data refers to a dataset comprising information related to diseases that affect a small percentage of the population. This data is used to evaluate the performance of DeepEnroll in handling and analyzing such specific and less common medical information."},
