{"matched_patients": "Matched patients refer to individuals who have been paired or grouped together based on specific criteria in a study or trial, such as the BLITZ Heart Failure trial.|Here is another description: Matched patients refer to individuals who have been identified as suitable candidates for participation in a specific trial based on predefined criteria. These patients have been selected because their characteristics align with the requirements of the trial, making them appropriate for inclusion in the study.|Here is another description: Matched patients refer to those individuals who have been identified as corresponding or fitting specific criteria within a trial or study. In the context of a heatmap, these patients are those whose data or characteristics align closely with the criteria set by the trial."},
{"matched_patients__are__highlighted": "The predicate \"are\" indicates a state of being or existence, suggesting that the matched patients possess a certain characteristic or are undergoing a particular process.|Here is another description: The predicate \"are\" serves as a linking verb in this context, connecting the subject \"Matched patients\" with their state or condition as being \"highlighted.\" It indicates that the matched patients possess the quality or state of being highlighted."},
