{"attention_weights__for__ec_statements_and_patient_pairs": "The predicate \"for\" in this context signifies the relationship between the attention weights and the EC statements and patient pairs. It indicates that the attention weights are calculated specifically for these elements to determine their relevance in the dataset."},
{"ec_statements_and_patient_pairs": "EC statements and patient pairs represent the data points being analyzed in the heatmap. EC statements include inclusion and exclusion criteria, while patient pairs refer to the patient embeddings being matched with these criteria. The relevance of these pairs is visualized through the attention weights, with darker colors indicating stronger relevance."},
