{"arxiv_preprint": "An arXiv preprint is a version of a scholarly or scientific paper that precedes formal peer review and publication in a peer-reviewed scholarly or scientific journal. The arXiv preprint in question is a document that presents the clinical BERT embeddings, detailing their development, methodology, and potential applications in the field of clinical natural language processing.|Here is another description: arXiv preprint is an online repository that hosts preprints of scientific papers across various fields, including physics, mathematics, computer science, and more. It allows researchers to share their work before it undergoes peer review and formal publication in a journal, facilitating rapid dissemination of new ideas and findings.|Here is another description: An arXiv preprint is a type of publication where scholarly articles, particularly in the fields of physics, mathematics, computer science, quantitative biology, quantitative finance, and statistics, are made available online before formal peer review and publication in a journal. The arXiv preprint for \"Deep contextualized word representations\" is identified by the arXiv identifier arXiv:1802.05365."},
